  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find all pairs of natural numbers $(m,n)$ for which $2mn=3m+6n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(m,n)=(4,6),(6,3),(12,2)$.\n\nUse $(m-3)(2n-3)=9$ and retain positive odd factor pairs.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}2mn-3m-6n&=0\\\\m(2n-3)-3(2n-3)-9&=0\\\\(m-3)(2n-3)&=9.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe original equation gives $m>3$ and $2n>3$. Thus\n\n$$(m-3,2n-3)=(1,9),(3,3),(9,1).$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$(m,n)=(4,6),(6,3),(12,2).$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
